{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot","id":39919,"title":"Camelot?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-31T05:42:55-08:00","id":39919,"title":"Camelot?","content":"I'm curious with what we have of Camelot. What I gather is that Merlin was an Acanthus Archmaster (probably Silver Ladder) that manipulated destinies and time to create an utopia. Eventually Camelot was erased from time by the Exarchs, but sparked lots of variant stories.<br /> <br /> But was it really erased? The variant stories and myths make it sound like it actually ascended. Was this Merlin's objective?<br /> <br /> I'm trying to picture a game set in Camelot. It might be awesome as hell. Perhaps making game sessions go back retroactively in time? It starts with the erasing/ascension of Camelot, and players work back to decide if it's getting erased or ascending. They might work with or against Merlin.<br /> <br /> What more do we have on Camelot? There is Mordred, in Astral Realms. But that's all I can think of.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T06:23:33-08:00","id":39932,"title":"","content":"It's only a model.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T07:37:55-08:00","id":39972,"title":"","content":"Indeed, Dave, 'tis a silly place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","name":"Raikirah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T09:24:29-08:00","id":40026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=39932#post39932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's only a model.</div> </div> </div> </div>But for what? :O<br /> <br /> Or is this a reference I'm not getting? :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T09:27:47-08:00","id":40028,"title":"","content":"He's referencing <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m3dZl3yfGpc\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1446-raikirah","name":"Raikirah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T09:53:25-08:00","id":40042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot#post39919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">players work back to decide if it's getting erased or ascending.</div> </div> </div> </div> I always thought that it did neither; Camelot turned into a story (in this reality, who knows what it will be after the next Archmaster mucks around; I'm under the impression that so long as Camelot is mentioned in the Supernal, and it's mentioned in one of Merlin's symbols, it has to exist in some form and it just happens to be in the form of a fictional place right now. If it was ever removed entirely from the Supernal it would end up in the Abyss).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T12:41:35-08:00","id":40112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=40042#post40042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I always thought that it did neither; Camelot turned into a story (in this reality, who knows what it will be after the next Archmaster mucks around; I'm under the impression that so long as Camelot is mentioned in the Supernal, and it's mentioned in one of Merlin's symbols, it has to exist in some form and it just happens to be in the form of a fictional place right now. If it was ever removed entirely from the Supernal it would end up in the Abyss).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. Still, I would like to know more. Sounds like a pretty big achievement even for an Archmaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T13:11:47-08:00","id":40121,"title":"","content":"Merlin created a Utopia using long-term manipulations of Fate and Destiny as his Omens - his Noumenon was to establish a destined link between a king and the land, and he Ascended (his body turning into the crystal cave) when the Bane of all those destinies came true.<br /> <br /> At which point, the whole damn thing was promptly erased from the timeline by the Ruin. But no matter what the Exarchs do, Arthurian symbols resonate with the Acanthus, and the Aeon of Fate transformed from the Greek Triple-Fates into Mordred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T13:17:52-08:00","id":40124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=40112#post40112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice. Still, I would like to know more. Sounds like a pretty big achievement even for an Archmaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems standard for an Archmaster. Anything that you seal in an Omen will always survive reality rewrites, but maybe not in it's original form.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T04:18:45-08:00","id":40448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=40042#post40042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it was ever removed entirely from the Supernal it would end up in the Abyss).</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't that imply that there exist in the Abyss, completely harmless fragments of reality which would not damage the tapestry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T06:13:44-08:00","id":40479,"title":"","content":"I imagine that the persistence of Camelot is similar to the whole deal with the eternal resonance of the Orders, namely that Merlin's Ascended status gives it a measure of sacrosanctity even if the more vulgar qualities of it are consigned to non-existence or Paradox.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't that imply that there exist in the Abyss, completely harmless fragments of reality which would not damage the tapestry?</div> </div> </div> </div>Things from the Abyss damage the world because they're not supposed to exist here and the processes that allow them to contradictorily exist are themselves damaging. It's like a form of reality metastasis.<br /> <br /> Although, given the inherently paradoxical nature of Abyssal phenomena, things which by all rights should seem harmless will have damaging qualities (and things which seem like they should be damaging will have contradictory helpful properties, which unfortunately don't interface with reality in a way that really mitigates the damaging properties, so being stabbed with a Healing Shiv will leave a perfectly healthy bled-out corpse).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T12:40:57-08:00","id":41246,"title":"","content":"Couldn't Camelot be another example of &quot;If Atlantis existed in some other time and was erased from history&quot;? After all, it's another mythical utopia where everything was grand all thanks to powerful wizards and great kings and they'll all be coming back when the world has finally dropped as low as it can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T13:17:22-08:00","id":41282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=40479#post40479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things from the Abyss damage the world because they're not supposed to exist here and the processes that allow them to contradictorily exist are themselves damaging. It's like a form of reality metastasis.<br /> <br /> Although, given the inherently paradoxical nature of Abyssal phenomena, things which by all rights should seem harmless will have damaging qualities (and things which seem like they should be damaging will have contradictory helpful properties, which unfortunately don't interface with reality in a way that really mitigates the damaging properties, so being stabbed with a Healing Shiv will leave a perfectly healthy bled-out corpse).</div> </div> </div> </div>Better way to describe it is to think of the world as Source Code which has been heavily rewritten to serve the programmer's purpose. It suffered it's first massive rewrite via the Exarchs/Oracles in which leaves the world as it currently is. <br /> <br /> However, the garbage code is never really purge but instead commented out. If circumstances are created to have contradictory code (Line 3552 says Magic exists. Line 5554 says Magic does not exist) then paradox occurs (much like a program throwing an exception) and garbage code is allowed into the program which may or may not bring up objects that have been previously deleted or objects which shouldn't exist at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> All this goes to show you that Mages really suck at debugging/developing, the lanague that they are using needs a garbage collector, and the System Administrator needs to get a back bone and tell them to test their programs before allowing them to be thrown into production.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T13:44:20-08:00","id":41298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=41246#post41246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't Camelot be another example of &quot;If Atlantis existed in some other time and was erased from history&quot;? After all, it's another mythical utopia where everything was grand all thanks to powerful wizards and great kings and they'll all be coming back when the world has finally dropped as low as it can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes indeed, it could - and Mages in Dark Ages Britain probably <i>did</i> ascribe Arthurian (pre-Romancification) origins to what modern Mages would call Atlantean remnants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T02:08:18-08:00","id":41589,"title":"","content":"In fact, and I feel okay with telling you this, but that setting was the one of the two I came up with for Dark Eras that we <i>didn't</i> end up writing. <br /> <br /> Dark Ages Britain, replacing &quot;Atlantis&quot; with &quot;Arthurian Britain&quot; as the origin for the inexplicable mysteries and stripping all the Romantic era additions from the myths. It'd be Arthurian as in &quot;grinning blood-soaked warlord&quot; Arthur, stone circles built by giants, probably-not-allegorical dragons, remnants of the old religion, pugnacious Christian saints and all.<br /> <br /> Just like Atlantis never happened in the modern-day setting but mages encounter evidence of it, the setting would be the real Dark Ages - and unlike other games we've made in the past would <i>actually</i> be set in the Dark Ages, not several centuries later - but with the ahistorical magical remnants of Arthurian Britain poking up from the seams.<br /> <br /> Naturally, a few days after I pitched it I found a FATE game called Age of Arthur that hits the same &quot;anti-Pendragon&quot; spot I was aiming for. C'est La Vie. The setting that won out for Dark Eras is more &quot;a very interesting period from Awakening's history that highlights its themes&quot; than &quot;Awakening's themes transplanted to an alien time, largely disconnected from the gameline&quot;, so I believe we've made the right decision.<br /> <br /> Camelot will just go on being an occassionally-mentioned cool bit in Awakening's setting lore.<br /> <br /> It's cropped up recently in our discussions for Fallen World Chronicle, actually. We were talking about how we want the Acanthus to shift in presentation from &quot;effortless and unconcerned&quot; to &quot;schemers who see possible futures and then manipulate events to go down their preferred ones&quot; - passive characters to proactive ones. The first two exemples of characters we're thinking of for the nuAcanthus? Paul Mau'dib from Dune... And Merlin.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":21}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T04:35:06-08:00","id":41640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=41589#post41589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We were talking about how we want the Acanthus to shift in presentation from &quot;effortless and unconcerned&quot; to &quot;schemers who see possible futures and then manipulate events to go down their preferred ones&quot; - passive characters to proactive ones. The first two exemples of characters we're thinking of for the nuAcanthus? Paul Mau'dib from Dune... And Merlin.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>How oddly fortuitious that I should be watching The Vision of Escaflowne at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T05:27:21-08:00","id":41653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=41589#post41589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, and I feel okay with telling you this, but that setting was the one of the two I came up with for Dark Eras that we <i>didn't</i> end up writing.<br /> <br /> Dark Ages Britain, replacing &quot;Atlantis&quot; with &quot;Arthurian Britain&quot; as the origin for the inexplicable mysteries and stripping all the Romantic era additions from the myths. It'd be Arthurian as in &quot;grinning blood-soaked warlord&quot; Arthur, stone circles built by giants, probably-not-allegorical dragons, remnants of the old religion, pugnacious Christian saints and all.<br /> <br /> Just like Atlantis never happened in the modern-day setting but mages encounter evidence of it, the setting would be the real Dark Ages - and unlike other games we've made in the past would <i>actually</i> be set in the Dark Ages, not several centuries later - but with the ahistorical magical remnants of Arthurian Britain poking up from the seams.<br /> <br /> Naturally, a few days after I pitched it I found a FATE game called Age of Arthur that hits the same &quot;anti-Pendragon&quot; spot I was aiming for. C'est La Vie. The setting that won out for Dark Eras is more &quot;a very interesting period from Awakening's history that highlights its themes&quot; than &quot;Awakening's themes transplanted to an alien time, largely disconnected from the gameline&quot;, so I believe we've made the right decision.<br /> <br /> Camelot will just go on being an occassionally-mentioned cool bit in Awakening's setting lore.<br /> <br /> It's cropped up recently in our discussions for Fallen World Chronicle, actually. We were talking about how we want the Acanthus to shift in presentation from &quot;effortless and unconcerned&quot; to &quot;schemers who see possible futures and then manipulate events to go down their preferred ones&quot; - passive characters to proactive ones. The first two exemples of characters we're thinking of for the nuAcanthus? Paul Mau'dib from Dune... And Merlin.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would love to play this. Same game as Awakening, diferent feel. Maybe some Orders differences. Months ago, when I was trying to picture a Dark Ages Mage and thought it wasn't sufficiently differently from the regular game, this was my answer.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I love the idea of the Alexander setting, too. The origins of the Orders and the Seers (maybe we might see the Aegis Kai Doru, too?). How not to love that? It's like Mage's Requiem for Rome. But maybe we might see this one, too? Perhaps as a stretch goal for Dark Eras, perhaps another book down the line? Dark Eras surely will measure the popularity of historical settings, and if very popular, might spawn other similar books. Perhaps a proper Dark Ages book? (To go along my dream of Viking Werewolves). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And really, the fact that a game line goes for the same source shouldn't really be a problem. Different settings and mechanics will lead to different games.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also,dragons! It would be really cool to see a remnant of them. It's possible that not all of them ascended, but it would be really hard for one to be alive today. Hope we get to see one in the Alexander setting, at least.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":196,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","user":"Max Deltree","date":". 01-03-2014, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T07:28:14-08:00","id":41698,"title":"","content":"DaveB, stop. Stop it right now. First you talk about putting a WoD setting in Arthurian post-Roman Britain, my favorite period of history that isn't helped by my love of Greg Stafford's games, and <i>then</i> you mention <b>Dune</b>?<br /> <br /> Depression-era Promethean and turn-of-the-century tomb-robbery Mummy is more than I can handle as it is","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T09:44:57-08:00","id":41794,"title":"","content":"If you walk without rhythm you won 't attract the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T19:25:22-08:00","id":1038702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/39919-camelot?p=41589#post41589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, and I feel okay with telling you this, but that setting was the one of the two I came up with for Dark Eras that we <i>didn't</i> end up writing. <br